Engine
- vLLM (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm), Apache-2.0. The image is
  upstream vLLM's wheel for commit a0d7356b98, the fork's DeepSeek-V4.1 vLLM
  branch over it and the vllm-cmp170hx plugin, all from
  https://github.com/AlexBrandes/vllm, also Apache-2.0 (see that repository's
  NOTICE), on NVIDIA's CUDA 13.0 Ubuntu 24.04 base image.
- The plugin's EXL3 codec is adapted from turboderp's ExLlamaV3
  (https://github.com/turboderp-org/exllamav3), MIT (copy in
  licenses/ExLlamaV3.LICENSE).
- The plugin's layout, startup guard and seam tooling are derived from
  vllm-sm80 by Morrowmake (https://github.com/Morrowmake/vllm-cmp170hx),
  Apache-2.0.

Model
- DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 by DeepSeek, MIT (copy in
  licenses/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash.LICENSE). The checkpoint
  codebrandes/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017-A4NX-2.2bpw and its INT8 dense weights
  are derivatives under the same licence. It was converted with a fork of
  turboderp's ExLlamaV3 (https://github.com/AlexBrandes/exllamav3, branch
  a4nx at 6cfd44b2, MIT).
- The Engram tables are DeepSeek's own files; download.sh fetches them from
  deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017.
- This repository ships no weights: download.sh fetches the checkpoint and the
  Engram tables from their model pages.

Benchmarks
- Speed tables use the sparkDash protocol (MiaAI-Lab/sparkDash, commit
  3e6d4ef, Apache-2.0); its prompts are used as data with attribution.
- GSM8K (OpenAI, MIT) as distributed with vLLM's tests/evals/gsm8k; HumanEval+
  (EvalPlus, Apache-2.0; HumanEval by OpenAI, MIT); IFEval (Google, Apache-2.0)
  with its instruction checkers; MMLU (Hendrycks et al., MIT); RULER (NVIDIA,
  Apache-2.0).
- Distance from the original: WikiText-2 (Merity et al., CC BY-SA 3.0).

